 "relevance_note": "Narrative review of paediatric Behçet's disease; the only individual-level HA20 mention is a previously published patient with a stated feature: 'a patient treated for longstanding intestinal BD-like symptoms was later diagnosed with A20 haploinsufficiency [91]'.",
 "method_note": "Read the whole paper by hand; no table transcribed by script (a script only assembled the JSON). All other HA20 mentions are group-level (Zhou et al. [13] five families; [41] 16 patients; [89] 'familial BD patients'; [33] cohort including A20 haploinsufficiency) and give no individual-level facts, so they get no rows. Table 3 'HA 20' column is disease-level, not per person. The ref [91] patient is included under the v4 passing-mention rule because a feature (longstanding intestinal BD-like symptoms) is given; this is borderline. No variant row: the paper gives this person an HA20 diagnosis but does not itself tie a TNFAIP3 variant to the person or print one. 'intestinal BD-like symptoms' was not mapped to the checklist item 'gastrointestinal ulcers or inflammation' because ulcers/inflammation are not stated. cites_prior_report_of_same_patients left null: the review has no first-hand patients. first_author taken as 'Kul Cinar' from the header 'Kul Cinar Ovgu' (author contributions use 'O.K.C.'). No contradictions found.",
